 "r32_miss_diagnosis": "The earlier script passed the lepton masses in MeV (0.511, 105.66) into dl(m, b, M) while b=200 and M=1e4 are in GeV, so y=m/b was 1000 times too large and the amplitudes were r_mu ~ 1.0 instead of 0.023, giving delta_mu - delta_e = 4.6e-5 (reproduced here to the digit). With masses in GeV the same eq. (22)-style formula gives the printed amplitudes and the closed form -(delta_mu - delta_e)/2 = -0.105 ppm, so the printed W value stands and the factor ~200 was a unit slip, not a formula error."
